# Resource-loading half of the edge Content-Security-Policy, enforced.
#
# 40-biotron-sites.sh fills ${BASE_DOMAIN} in the policy line at the bottom
# once per instance in EDGE_SITES and maps each domain to its own policy, so
# every instance names only its own product subdomains. nginx.conf sends the
# mapped value as Content-Security-Policy at http level, beside the
# deployment-independent document-level policy; a browser enforces both, so
# they add up rather than override each other. An unknown host gets no
# header. Lines starting with # are left out of the header.
#
# SCRIPTS. Each tool's index.html carries the same inline theme bootstrap,
# which AGENTS.md keeps there so the dark theme applies before React loads.
# The five copies are byte-identical, so one SHA-256 hash allows them all and
# no other inline script: an injected <script> or event handler does not run.
# Editing the bootstrap changes its hash. infra/tests checks that every inline
# script of every index.html matches the hash below; compute a new one with
#
#   perl -0ne 'print $1 while /<script>(.*?)<\/script>/sg' apps/auth/frontend/index.html |
#     openssl dgst -sha256 -binary | openssl base64
#
# and keep the copies identical. .gitattributes keeps index.html LF, as the
# hash assumes.
#
# STYLES keep 'unsafe-inline': React writes style attributes throughout, and
# each index.html has a small <style>. A style cannot run code.
#
# Violations are reported to the edge (report-uri, report-to), which logs
# them: see snippets/csp-report.conf.
#
# The directives were derived by reading what the apps actually load, and
# checked by browsing every app with the policy enforced:
#   script-src              same-origin Vite bundles and the hashed bootstrap.
#   style-src               the inline <style> in each index.html, plus React
#                           inline style attributes.
#   img-src                 same-origin assets, Vite's inlined data: URIs,
#                           blob: textures of the site's 3D models, and GitHub
#                           avatars (operator.avatar_url is rendered in the
#                           account menu of all four authenticated apps).
#   font-src                Tailwind ships no webfont and no frontend links
#                           Google Fonts; data: covers any future inlined face.
#   connect-src             each frontend calls its own API and, cross-origin,
#                           auth.${BASE_DOMAIN}; the public site and Sprinter
#                           call the calendar API. Enumerated, not wildcarded.
#                           https://raw.githack.com, which redirects to
#                           raw.githubusercontent.com, serves the HDR lighting of
#                           the site's 3D scenes: drei's <Environment preset>
#                           fetches it from there. Self-hosting those files
#                           would let this origin go.
#   worker-src blob:        Three.js loaders on the public site construct their
#                           decoder workers from blobs.
#   frame-src 'none'        no frontend embeds an iframe.
#   report-uri, report-to   the edge logs each violation.
default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-SRsBKnFT7raAfsMsc1moMQx0K/6SZ+7uvHVQ8YD2kQo='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://avatars.githubusercontent.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://${BASE_DOMAIN} https://www.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://auth.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://exogui.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://status.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://calendar.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://sprinter.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://raw.githack.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'; report-uri /_edge/csp-report; report-to csp
